SOAPBOX: This is our 32nd consecutive CQWW SSB at V26B (except the covid year). We might be the longest running group out there.
SOAPBOX: It is a lot of hard work maintaining and operating a big station in the Caribbean heat and sun, which can be brutal at times. After the hard work comes the fun, and we had a blast again this year. Conditions favored us and the results will show that. Probably the last good year for the next few years.
SOAPBOX: We only had 7 ops this year, but this is a seasoned bunch and they get better every year.
SOAPBOX: It's an honor to operate with these gentlemen: K3RA, AA3R, KC2GOW, NM2O, K3MTT and N2ZN. I love you guys.
SOAPBOX: Raising hell from two-point land,
SOAPBOX: For TEAM ANTIGUA:
SOAPBOX: Brian N3OC
SOAPBOX: Chief bottle washer and part-time rotator fixer
